WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.980
I've finished checking the passengers.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:08.900
None of them seem to be
showing any of the symptoms.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.570
Nor do any of them have a fever or any injuries.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.450
Nor are they already dead.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.120
Your family lives in Tokyo?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.160
No one answered the phone...

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.000
<i>Tokonosu Tower, JX089.
Ready for take off.</i>

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.640
<i>JX089, Tokonosu Tower.
Hold on runway 3-4.</i>

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.890
<i>We have a...</i>

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.430
<i>problem.</i>

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:06.540
Yureta Genjitsukan Nakushita Mama de

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:06.540
As I lose my already shaken touch with reality,

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:11.630
Gareki no Youni Tsumikasanaru

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:11.630
my emotions pile up like fallen debris

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.880
Kono Kanshou wa Doko e Yuku

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.880
Where do they think they're going?

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.180
Tsuieta Kibou Kakae

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.180
With my crushed hope in tow,

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.100
Akai Ame o Harai Hashitta Muchuu ni

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.100
I ran straight through the bloody rain

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:32.780
Kuzureta Kanjou no Hate ni

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:32.780
After my emotions come spilling out,

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.070
Nani o Miru

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.070
what will I see?

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.360
Nani ga Aru

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.360
What will I have?

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.030
Mada Shiranai

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.030
I still don't know

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:42.910
Hakanai Subete no Minori wa

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:42.910
But in this silence,

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.500
Tada Muon ni Me no Mae ni

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.500
all of the shallow things I could gain

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:52.500
Hirogari Tsudzuketa

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:52.500
lie endlessly before me

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.830
He looks repulsive.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.920
He's an actor.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.050
He was on location here for filming.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.510
Distance: 4500.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.510
Angle: -6.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.510
Wind: Favorable.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.350
Corrections: None.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.270
Permission to fire: Granted.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.490
Good work.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.620
All of the targets on the runway have been eliminated.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:11.580
Over and out.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.000
What're you doing?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.420
These things are numb. I've been laying down here since this morning.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.010
If you don't mind, I could massage them.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.520
I would if you were a better shot than me.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.400
But you're one of the top five officers in our whole country.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.360
That's no fair.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.020
You'd better give up then.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.070
Anyway...

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.740
How did those things even get here? We're at a seaside airport that can only be reached by ship.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.200
Haven't they been restricting entry?

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.330
Yeah.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:51.830
Only high ranking officials and airport technicians as well as their families are allowed in.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.130
One of them must've been infected.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.510
The situation is under control right now, but who knows how long that'll last?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.600
What do you think would've happened to this place

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.520
if we hadn't been assigned here due to terrorist threats?

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:14.100
Well, I don't have infinite ammo...

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.650
You're gonna run away?

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.480
Not planning on it.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:20.320
Well, not yet.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.700
I'm gonna go to the city.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.450
Eventually.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.370
What, you have a guy there?

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.830
Naw, a friend.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.750
That's right.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:42.920
Thus, instead of acting out of self-interest,

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.970
we need to find a safe place and move as a group.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.720
For example, we shouldn't all go check on our families

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:56.100
until we become an organized group.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:59.940
In fact, I think the number one thing for us right now

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.570
Hirano.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.610
is laying down a foundation for our group.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.110
Understand?

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:02.990
Takagi...

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.530
Good morning, sunshine.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.530
Why did you fall asleep?

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:07.950
And you're drooling!

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.500
Because of... all this.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.420
I think it would've been better if we had gone toward the suburbs.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.510
There are other ways to escape besides cars.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.930
The seaside airport?

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:31.510
As you can see, it's too dangerous to be in the city.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.730
There's probably a group of people who are trying to flee to an island

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.850
or to some isolated area where there are armed forces.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.230
Like Okinawa?

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.940
The American military forces that're stationed there aren't there to fight.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.240
Oh, but there is the SDF...

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:53.240
Hokkaido and Kyushu should be okay if they handled the situation appropriately.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.250
I'd say the airplanes are headed for one of those locations.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.920
So we should go somewhere like that too?

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.000
It's way too late for that.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.510
Areas with large amounts of American soldiers or where the SDF is stationed

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.680
are probably keeping the situation under control.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.390
However, it's likely that they started being strict about who they take in.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:16.430
Actually, before we know it, the whole world will be like that.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:23.110
What would you do if letting in others meant risking letting those things in too?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.440
I'd shut myself in.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.320
And what if the whole world started thinking the same as you?

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:38.080
What if they tried to keep their community as small as possible for maximum survival?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.000
Wow Takagi, you really are a genius.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.300
What're you acting so surprised about?

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:47.840
Just look at him. He's an example of what I'm talking about.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.430
But I doubt that he himself realizes it.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:55.810
I mean, you know what happened overnight.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.980
Should I stop him?

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:03.650
What we should be doing is thinking about how we're going to survive.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.690
I need someone I can trust...

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:10.450
Jeez, if only Komuro were here.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.910
Takagi, you like Komuro, don't you?

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.370
Don't say something so stupid!

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.290
W-What?

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.420
I am concerned about their safety.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.880
It would be preferable if we were able to meet them without incident.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.360
Shit's awesome! It looks like Hell!

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.570
This is crazy. It's like a war.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.370
This might be worse than a war...

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.990
It's too dangerous here.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:58.040
I'm gonna go through it.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.710
Hey!

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:09.840
Hang on!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.600
Why are they trying to kill us? We're still human!

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.860
They're going mad.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.110
Just like we are.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:32.070
Like we are?

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.160
Huh? Isn't the bridge straight ahead?

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.000
Look at the other side of the bridge.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:52.340
Who knows when we'll be able to cross over.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.680
Let's go toward Onbetsu Bridge and try to meet up with the others.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:07.730
I repeat!

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:13.150
Please stay calm and continue to follow the polices' instructions!

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:19.620
Currently, city wide traffic has been restricted.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:24.330
Any unauthorized persons who attempt to cross the river will be reprimanded.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.540
Additionally, crossing by foot is also prohibited.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.800
Hey! Wait!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.720
You were looking at her panties, weren't you?!

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.300
Hey, move it!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.140
Shut up, granny!

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:41.680
Move it!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.680
Attention, students!

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:46.390
Do not attempt to cross the bridge!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.440
This is our final warning!

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.310
Don't give me that shit!

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.440
As if we'd listen to the cops!

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:55.530
Who needs them when we've got the juvenile law?!

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.360
You're so cool, Hide~!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:00.780
Releasing water!

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.670
M-Mr. Officer, they made me...

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:16.800
Releasing water!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.180
As members of Fujimi Academy,

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:31.190
it's during trying times like these that we must keep our pride!

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:43.240
We must keep our pride!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:51.670
Meaning those two who got off the bus, Komuro and Miyamoto, don't belong with us anyway!

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.800
Let's stick together in order to survive!

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.630
He's seriously insane.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:11:00.510
Let us work together and triumph!

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.380
Indeed.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:02.140
He is comparable to a recruitment officer for a religious cult.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.140
Mr. Shido!

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.470
Comparable to? No, that's exactly what he's doing.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.930
Just look at the people who are listening to his crap.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.890
They're a cult...

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:15.110
This marks the birth of the Shido Religion.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.440
Look at the situation outside.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.610
In order to escape, I believe we will need to leave this bus.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:25.530
Somehow, we must make it to the east police station by means of crossing Onbetsu Bridge.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.740
I must keep my promise to meet Komuro there.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.460
Wow, you really have Komuro on your mind.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:34.170
You aren't worried about your family?

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:40.220
I do worry, but the only kin I have is my father. He is overseas at a dojo.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:47.350
As such, all I have to hold onto right now is my life and my promise with Komuro.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:49.930
Father has always taught me

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:54.230
that a promise must be kept even if it should cost you your life.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:58.820
Where do you all live?

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:02.110
My house is in the same area as Komuro's on the other side of Onbetsu Bridge.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:05.660
Uhm, my parents aren't in the neighborhood,

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.620
but I'll follow Takagi to the end of the world.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.040
Gross!

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:14.170
Where is your family, Hirano?

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:18.840
My dad is in Amsterdam buying supplies since he's a jewel merchant.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:22.550
My mom is a fashion designer and she's been in Paris...

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.050
What the?! What time period is this character sheet from?

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:31.560
If we were in a manga, your dad would be the captain of a foreign cruise ship.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.850
Actually, that was my grandpa.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.560
My grandma was a violinist.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.030
I-It all fits...

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:42.690
So, what are you guys gonna do?

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.070
I wanna come too.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.620
You do?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:50.990
My parents are both dead and my relatives live far away.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:57.000
It's rude of me to say this, but I don't really like Mr. Shido.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.880
Then what shall we do?

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.760
This area is foreign to me.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.880
First, we'll check on Onbetsu Bridge.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.050
What's wrong, you guys?

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.560
We should work together.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:13.850
Thanks but no thanks, Mr. Shido.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:17.400
We've got our own agenda.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:22.190
We're not on a field trip, so we have no reason to stay with you.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:24.900
Oh?

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:35.870
If you've decided to leave, then feel free to do so, Takagi.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:40.710
Japan is the land of the free after all.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:42.550
But...

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.930
It'd be bad if you went, Ms. Marikawa.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:53.890
In this situation, losing our medic would be very problematic.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:56.060
So, how about it?

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.940
Won't you stay?

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:03.110
These students are relying on you.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.160
Hi-Hirano?

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.410
It's not that I missed.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.750
I missed on purpose.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.120
S-Since when have you been so viol--

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.630
How many corpses do you think I wrecked back at school?

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.710
You know,

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:27.920
you've always treated me like crap!

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.090
But I put up with it.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:34.640
I put up with it for so long!

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.930
I wanted to be normal,

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.400
so I kept putting up with it!

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:45.530
But I don't need to do that anymore.

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:48.200
Normal doesn't mean shit!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.740
That's why...

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.950
I can kill.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:56.500
I can kill the living too.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:01.500
H-Hirano, t-that's...

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:05.130
Busujima-sempai, you should get off first.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.840
I'll guard the rear!

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.340
What a fine man you are, Hirano.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:20.850
Teacher?

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.230
It's the same here.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.440
Now what?

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.450
Check on a different bridge?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.320
That sounds pointless.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.990
I bet all of the bridges have been blocked.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:38.450
Otherwise, there's no reason for the police to be there.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.960
Somehow, we need to get across Onbetsu Bridge

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.420
and get to the east police station by 7 PM.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:50.050
But how?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.300
Lemme think!

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:54.550
Right now, I wish--

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:55.720
Don't say it!

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.520
Even if you do, things won't change.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.060
Gunshots?

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.650
No, that's...

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:12.990
M-M-Maybe it would've been better if we had stayed on the bus with Mr. Shido!

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:16.490
What's that? I thought you said you hated him?

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:21.910
Well, I really don't like him, but I don't like walking either.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.500
Busujima-sempai, I'm low on nails!

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.470
Would you like to borrow this?

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:36.090
I'm no good at close range combat!

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.720
Right now...

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:42.100
The only thing I can do is fight!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:47.610
Wait a sec...

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.650
Takashi?

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.160
Nooo!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:58.830
Takagi!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.040
Damn!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.040
Komuro!

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.030
Double tap!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.380
Busujima-sempai!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.640
Wow...

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:05.230
It seems we have cleared this area.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.980
Wow that was tough!

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.360
It's not like you did anything...

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:11.610
Teacher!

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:15.530
Oh my, Miyamoto! What a goincidence!

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:19.030
...don't you mean coincidence?

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.870
Komuro too!

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.910
I take it that Tokonosu Bridge is also closed off.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.870
Yup. There's nowhere to go.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.330
In that case,

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.250
I am glad to see that you are okay, Komuro.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.340
You too, Busujima-sempai.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.010
And what about me?

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:38.010
Uh yeah nice to see you alive and well too, Takagi.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.010
And Hirano!

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.090
KOMURO~!

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.100
What's this?!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.140
How'd you get it?!

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:43.850
Bullets?

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:48.180
This is the same Smith & Wesson M37 Airweight that the police use, right?!

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.980
W-We can talk about it later...

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:50.520
This one is the Chief's Special...

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.400
We exited the bus due to the blocking of the road

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:58.400
and have been unable to cross the river.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.860
The water level went up.

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:03.530
I guess it wouldn't be possible to go upstream.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.740
So what should we do?

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.540
Uhm...

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:10.750
I think we should rest now.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.580
"Rest"?

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:17.590
You see, there's a place we can use. It's nearby, so we can walk there.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.130
Is it your boyfriend's?

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:23.430
N-No! It belongs to my female friend!

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:27.220
She's always busy and traveling because of work!

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.770
She gave me the key. I go over there while she's gone and let some fresh air in.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:34.400
Have a nice day~

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:36.570
Is it an apartment?

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.570
Is the view good?

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:39.780
Yeah!

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.700
It's a maisonette that's next to the river.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.820
It's close to a convenience store too.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:52.040
Oh, and she has a car too. It looks like a tank and it's thiiis big!

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:55.170
Well, I'm really tired.

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:57.800
I'd like to shower while there's still working electricity.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.800
S-Sounds good.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:02.880
You perv!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.100
We'll go check on it first.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.430
Get on, Ms. Shizuka.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:09.600
Okay!

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.980
The breeze is great!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:23.780
Uhm, teacher, you don't have to squeeze me...

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.950
Huh? What was that?

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.660
I can't hear you~

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:29.370
Uhm, I...

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.500
I can't hear you~

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.500
I...

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.870
I can't hear you~

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:37.420
I...

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:47.050
Hadazamui Yozora ni wa Kimi ga Omoiukabu

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:47.050
The chilly night sky makes me think of you

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:54.480
Shizukana Konna Hi ni wa Kimi ni Aitaku Naru

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:54.480
and the quiet day makes me want to see you

00:20:54.480 --> 00:21:03.190
Donna Hi mo Kimi no Koto Mamoritai Kara

00:20:54.480 --> 00:21:03.190
No matter what the day is like, I want to protect you

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:03.190
I want you baby

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:10.660
Hashiridashita Speed de Toozakatteku Hibi

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:10.660
The days that disappear at the same speed they appeared with

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:15.500
Tsunaida Te no Nukumori mo

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:15.500
and the warmth we felt in each others hands

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:19.540
Osanai Koro no Omoidebanashi

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:19.540
are just vestiges of our childhood

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:20.550
Time goes by

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:23.670
Kimi wa Mou Wasurete Shimatteirun Darou

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:23.670
I bet you've forgotten those things by now

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:27.260
Yubikiri Kawashita Yakusoku Sae mo

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:27.260
You probably forgot our promise too

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.890
Dakedo Mada Mune no Oku

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.890
I still have it in my heart

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.850
Nokosareta Kimochi ga

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.850
I won't ever be able to get rid of

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:35.980
Itsumademo Keshisarenai Mama

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:35.980
my remaining feelings for you

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:44.490
Hadazamui Yozora ni wa Kimi ga Omoiukabu

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:44.490
The chilly night sky makes me think of you

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:51.870
Shizukana Konna Hi ni wa Kimi ni Aitaku Naru

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:51.870
and the quiet day makes me want to see you

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:58.540
Kurayami mo Surinukete Tonde Ikeru

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:58.540
I can fly to you while passing through darkness

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:00.130
I can fly for you

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:09.010
Ano Koro to Kawaranai Boku no Mama de

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:09.010
Just like I did back then

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:08.680
I want you baby

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:21.520
It's a Hum-Vee! And a military model at that!

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:23.900
See? Doesn't it look like a tank?

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:26.490
What kind of friend do you have?

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:29.240
I bet those things can't jump the fence.

00:22:29.240 --> 00:22:31.490
We should be able to sleep peacefully.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:33.540
Anyway, we should hurry--

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.420
How's this, Komuro?

00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:43.250
It's good enough.

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:44.500
Stay back.

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.010
Remember to cover for one another.

00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:50.260
Let's go!

00:22:52.300 --> 00:22:54.390
<i>Thinking back on it,</i>

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:56.390
<i>the way in which we changed was surprising.</i>

00:22:57.350 --> 00:23:00.900
<i>At that time, we didn't run away.</i>

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:06.610
<i>In order to survive, we quit running away and started attacking.</i>

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:11.200
<i>And none of us stopped to question ourselves.</i>

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:13.950
<i>We had changed...</i>

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:15.950
<i>We had changed so much</i>

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:19.750
<i>in just a day.</i>

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:28.590
Woah, teach...

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:35.890
Keep going and we'll be in trouble.
